ed margin  This area is the largest firm area found in the specimen is located near a blue inked area  Within the axillary tail are multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm  Two of the lymph nodes appear to contain yellow material  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A F  Possible whole lymph nodes found in the axillary tail with D and F containing yellow material within the lymph node G  First described nodule and margin H  Second described nodule and margin I  Third described nodule and margin J  Fourth described nodule and margin K L  Main mass and closest margin respectively M N  Representative sections of normal appearing breast in lateral portion of the specimen S  Additional possible lymph node Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node tissue  is a 3 x 2 5cm portion of red to yellow soft tissue which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm portion of matted lymph nodes which is bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes O P  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm fatty tissue which is dissected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm tan tissue  The specimen is bivalved to reveal a homogenous tan cut section  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette Q  The remaining tissue is submitted in cassette R  Resident  VINCENT KO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  WEI LIEN WANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES LEFT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  