d by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right segmental mastectomy  re excision of tumor site  is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 2 1cm fibrofatty breast tissue with an overlying skin ellipse measuring 4 x 1 7cm  The skin surface is white tan with blue sentinel node ink  There is a 2 5cm scar at the center of the skin ellipse  The specimen has two stitches present which are designated one stitch superior and two stitches medial  The specimen is oriented and inked as follows  black superior  blue inferior  orange superficial anterior  yellow deep  posterior   The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial revealing a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic cavity and comes to within 0 5cm of the superior margin and 1 5cm of the skin surface  In addition near the lateral edge there is a 0 4cm clear cyst that comes to within 0 4cm of the superior margin  Cross sections of the specimen are submitted in from lateral to medial in cassettes A P  block F O contain the cavity   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted in cassette Q  Resident  CHAD SOUPIR  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  VINCENT KO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  RIGHT SEGMENTAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL  , Multifocal.
