n  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast tissue  A short stitch designates the anterior surface  a long stitch designates the lateral surface and a bow tie stitch designates the cephalad surface  The specimen is linked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass that is 0 5cm from the deep margin  1 5cm from the superior margin and 4 0cm from the inferior margin  1 4cm from the anterior margin  2 5cm from the lateral margin  and 2 5cm from the medial margin  The remainder of the breast shows fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section code  A  lateral margin  en face   B  medial margin  en face   C  mass with superior and anterior margins  D  mass with anterior margin  E  inferior margin  F  mass with posterior margin  G  additional section of mass  H  representative section of breast tissue away from mass  Q  lymph node adjacent to tumor Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue  Lymph nodes are identified and submitted as follows  I  whole lymph nodes  J  one lymph node  bisected  K  whole lymph nodes  L  two lymph nodes  bise