ins  This firm area surrounds a clip and is adjacent to a wire  No additional lesions or masses are appreciated  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from inferior to superior  with area of clip within blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections away from biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and   right breast  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular lobule of fibrofatty breast tissue  Cross section reveals predominately soft yellow lobulated fat interspersed with a small amount of dense to soft white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT DEEP   EXCISION , Multifocal_(multiple_within_same_quadrant).
