d their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy with needle localization  is a 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm yellow tan fibrofatty breast tissue with two wires in it  In addition  there are three sutures present which are designated short anterior  long lateral and bowtie cephalad  The specimen is oriented and the superior surface is inked blue  the inferior surface is inked black  the lateral surface is inked red and the medial surface is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior revealing a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white tan nodule that comes to within 1cm of the blue inked superior margin  The remainder of the cut sections show yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with white breast parenchyma and focal areas of hemorrhage  No other masses or abnormalities are noted  SECTION CODE A B  Blue inked margin and nodule C D  Nodule E F  Breast tissue adjacent to nodule G H  Breast parenchyma Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  primary sentinel node at 260  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow tan lymph node  The specimen is bisected to reveal a red tan cut surface with a 0 2cm white tan nodule at the edge of the lymph node  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  secondary SA at 100  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan lymph node  The specimen is bisected to reveal a red brown cut surface 