ONTH 96 at 10 43 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen reeptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 42     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  short superior  long lateral   is a piece of fatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  A well healed linear scar is present in the middle of the skin ellipse and measures 3 5cm  A long stitch marks the lateral aspect of the specimen  The short stitch marks the superior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is totally inked in black  and the superior aspect of the specimen is additionally inked in blue  Sectioning reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and approaching the inferior margin of the specimen on the lateral side to 0 4cm  The walls of the biopsy cavity consist of fibrous tissue  The biopsy cavity is submitted in toto in cassette A through H  beginning at the lateral margin and proceeding to the medial margin  The area of closest approach to the resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Cassettes I through K  representative section of the rest of the specimen  Cassette L  skin ellipse submitted in toto  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Lymph nodes are bisected and submitted in cassettes M through P  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  separate superior nodule  are three pieces of hard  white tan tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Submitted in toto in cassettes Q and R  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior margin  additional   short  new superior margin  long  lateral   is a piece of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The superior margin is marked by a short stitch  the lateral margin is marked by a long stitch  The specimen is inked in black in toto  The superior aspect is additionally inked in blue  The specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes S through Y  beginning at the lateral margin and proceeding to the medial margin  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART C  SEPARATE SUPERIOR NODULE  LEFT  PART D  SUPERIOR MARGIN ADDITIONAL   report_end  , Unifocal.
