jacent to the tip of the localization wire  The specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the anterior margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the posterior margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the cavity is  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the tissue adjacent to the tip of the localization wire as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the tissue containing the silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with attached axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  There an overlying elliptical portion of tan  wrinkled  hair bearing skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm  with a tan  wrinkled areola that measures 4 0cm in diameter and a pink brown  slightly flattened nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  There is a C shaped  slightly puckered area at the periphery of the areola measuring 3 0cm in length  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals three firm  stellate  ill defined masses in the central to lower inner quadrant measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  from lateral to medial   These areas are located 2 5cm from the posterior margin and 7 5cm from the anterior margin  7 5cm from the posterior margin and 3 0cm from the anterior margin  and 5 0cm from the posterior margin and 2 0cm from the anterior margin respectively  From lateral to medial  these areas are 3 2cm and 5 0cm from one another  There is a marked amount of nodular fibrous tissue at the periphery of these firm areas  The remaining cut surfaces consists predominantly of yellow  lobulated adipose tissue with a small amount of interspersed gray white fibrous tissue  The axillary tail is dissected and palpated to reveal multiple possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  The largest possible node is remarkable for gray yellow  focally hyperemic areas discoloration  There are multiple surgical clips noted at the periphery of this node  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Most lateral mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Between lateral and middle masses   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Middle mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Between middle and most medial masses   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Most medial mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular fibrous areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of uninvolved  from lower outer quadrant   with posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One representative section of largest lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing one possible lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible node  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes  submitted entirely  Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor 