Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 07 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING BOTH TISSUE FRAGMENTS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN MANY FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh for Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  are two fragments of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan white focally yellow slightly nodular cut surface  No area is grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Entirely submitted  The larger piece is in A J  and the smaller piece is in K M  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION  GROSS ONLY  NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 06 CLINICAL DATA  Firm left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  75   SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN IN TINY FOCI  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  25   OCCUPYING EIGHT OF ELEVEN SECTIONS AND EXTENDING TO MANY MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion are not seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the slides and agrees with this interpretation  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ADENOSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  MICROCYSTS  AND FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 04 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue with short stitch on superior and long stitch on lateral margin  Lateral margin is inked red  the remainder inked black  The tissue is serially sectioned from superior to inferior  Sectioning reveals a 1 0cm stellate  tan  firm area with a central depression  Representative sections frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The rest of the breast parenchyma is submitted in A through K  with the firm stellate area in C through F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the new inferior margin  The new inferior margin is inked red and the remaining tissue is inked black  submitted entirely in L through O  medially to laterally  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                 