s stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue level 1  REMOVED_CASE_ID   are three fragments of tan yellow soft tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The largest fragment of tissue is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is submitted as cassette B  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  wide excision left breast mass  short stitch superior long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 ocm portion of breast tissue with a short suture and long suture  The specimen is black inked anterior and blue inked posterior  and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white gritty partially well defined mass adjacent to the mid superior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma has a multiple ill defined tan white fibrous focally gritty regions which partially abut the anterior lateral margin  C E  mass and adjacent closest margin F G  fibrous areas with adjacent posterior margin from mid to lateral H  ill defined fibrous area from the anterior lateral portion of the specimen  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margin inferior half of cavity are multiple fr