Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 07 CLINICAL DATA  Positive fine needle aspiration on left breast mass at MGH                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III  METASTATIC TO TWO OF ELEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   10     SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is 2cm  in greatest dimension  Lymphatic invasion is identified  Carcinoma is 0 7cm away from the closest resection margin  Inked resection margins are negative for tumor  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast mass  is a 5 x 4 x 2 8cm portion of breast parenchyma with two black sutures  The long suture designates the lateral aspect of the specimen while the short suture the superior  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan to brown scirrhous lesion with stellate radicals which extend out into the surrounding tissue  The tumor extends to within 0 7cm of the closest deep margin  which is 3 5cm medial to the lateral margin of the specimen  Within this specimen there are scattered foci of dense fibrosis  A representative section of such an area is taken  Tissue is taken for frozen section and saved frozen  Section Code A   closest deep margin B   additional deep margin C   closest superior margin D E   additional tumor F   representative section of fibrosis G   representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left axilla contents  is a 10 x 6 x 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 0 4cm aggregate of tan to red lymph nodes are dissected from the specimen and submitted with one of the nodes being suspicious for metastatic disease found in I  The remainder of the lymph nodes are found in H K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSSLY APPROACHING TO APPROXIMATELY 0 7CM FROM THE CLOSEST MA