uts the superior  red  margin  the posterior  black  margin and the inferior  yellow  margin  and is 0 6cm from the anterior  blue  margin  Within this region  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm focal area of punctate hemorrhage is identified consistent with previous core biopsy site  No other distinct masses are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODES  A  rubbery area to superior margin  B  core biopsy site  C  rubbery area to posterior margin  D  rubbery area to inferior margin  E  rubbery area to anterior margin  F G  parenchyma away from rubbery area N S  tissue from superior end of specimen T V  tissue surrounding second needle localization wire W II  additional sections from firm rubbery area Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassettes H I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node 460  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm lymph node  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  385  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node 200  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node 99  are 2 portions of adipose tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  submitted entirely in cassette M  Resident  HEIKE VARNHOLT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR