Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 05 CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma diagnosed by FNA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SPANNING APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE NOTE  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SPANNING APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  Two separate masses are present  one medial to nipple  3 4cm   that is composed entirely of high grade invasive carcinoma  the other lateral  3 0cm   that contains both in situ and invasive carcinoma of intermediate grade  The medial mass has a fairly well circumscribed border and may possibly represent complete replacement of an intraparenchymal lymph node  No definite blood vascular invasion is seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC HIGH GRADE ADENOCARCINOMA   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The axillary fat contained a 7 0cm mass representing numerous matted lymph nodes  It is impossible to determine the exact number of nodes involved  The adenocarcinoma is high grade and resembles the tumor in the medial mass  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   Lateral Nodule  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Breast  Left   Medial Nodule  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is an oriented mastectomy specimen  with a suture designating the superior aspect  The deep resection margin is inked black and the superior resection margin is inked blue  The mastectomy is overlaid by REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm ellipse of white pink skin  On its lateral aspect is a longitudinal 7 0cm long  well healed linear scar Sectioning through the breast parenchyma reveals at least two stellate irregular  firm nodular areas  located slightly superior to the nipple  The more lateral measures 3 0cm in greatest dimension and REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in cross section  It is white  firm stellate with central spiculation and located approximately 1 5cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  The second area is slightly more medial to the nipple and measures 3 4cm in greates