ived in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm skin ellipse  There is a single stitch designating the inferior and a double stitch designating the medial margins  The specimen is inked as follows  deep black  anterior blue  superior orange  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ill defined tan firm mass in the posterior inferior portion of the specimen abutting the inferior resection margin  0 1cm from the deep and superior resection margins  approximately 1 0cm from the medial margin  0 6cm from the anterior margin  and greater than 1 5cm from the lateral resection margins  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow and fatty with scant tan fibrosis  The mass is entirely submitted in cassette A F as follows  A medial margin enface  B  with inferior margin  C and D  inferior and anterior margins  E  inferior and deep margins  F  anterior  inferior and deep margins  Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Paula Arnell  M D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH A MINOR COMPONENT OF INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE AND NOTE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen focally  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  REMOVED_DATE MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Within the tumor mass are areas of necrosis and hemorrhage  The majority of the invasive and in situ carcinoma comprising the tumor mass demonstrate membrane staining with antibody to e cadherin  supporting the diagnosis of ductal carcinoma  There are areas at the periphery of the tumor  where the pattern of infiltration is more characteristic of lobular carcinoma  In these areas  the invasive tumor cells demonstrate weak to no e cadherin membrane staining  This  in addition to the fact that there is an associated in situ lobular carcinoma component  supports that a minor component of invasive lobular carcinoma is present  It is this lobular component that extends to   0 1cm from the posterior margin  Immunoperoxidase stains for p63 and smooth muscle myosin heavy chain show staining of myoepithelial cells around the in situ carcinoma  Immunoperoxidase stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and ULEX Europaeus help confirm the presence of lymphatic invasion  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm left simple mastectomy specimen  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm tan white unremarkable portion of skin with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect  The nipple areolar complex measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with an unremarkable nipple  No scar is grossly appreciated  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a lobulated  tan pink focally hemorrhagic indurated to rubbery mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  The mass is located within the mid to medial aspect of the specimen and comes to 1 0cm from the free moving overlying black inked posterior margin and 3 0cm from the unremarkable skin surface  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to pink  lobulated and unremarkable with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  Along the periphery no lymph nodes are palpated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass with the closest posterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show nuclear staining for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unifocal.
