nd eosin stained section  other immunostained sections  or still deeper sections that were subsequently obtained  Adjacent to this focus of microinvasive carcinoma is a second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ that is grade 1  A topographically separate second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ in the same section is grade 3  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Wyatt  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating axillary portion of the specimen  The anterior surface bears a 19 x 6cm tan brown skin ellipse  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 2 5cm linear well healed scar present approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position  3cm from the areola in the outer quadrant  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially bread loafed to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm fibrotic  calcified scar approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position in the outer quadrant beneath the overlying linear well healed scar on skin which lies 0 3cm from posterior and 2 4cm from overlying margin  Approximately 7cm medial to this scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity approximately between 6 and 7 o clock position  The biopsy cavity is lined a glistening lining and contain hemorrhagic material and a clip  The biopsy cavity lies 0 6cm from posterior and 5cm from overlying anterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma between the scar and the biopsy cavity contains predominantly tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma contains a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue admixed with tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is grossly appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  calcified scar  located between 1 and 3 o clock in the outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire biopsy cavity located between 6 and 7 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma intervening the scar and the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  outer quadrant  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 06 51PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Amendment  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 07 52AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The invasive tumor cells and the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1  stain for estrogen receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for progesterone receptor protein and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not show the invasive tumor cells or the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1   The second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 3  do not stain for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins  and HER 2 c erbB 2  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 41 47PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 AUG 97 at 14 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FIELD FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   Note  Definite ductal carcinoma in situ  and blood vascular and lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 18 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 AUG 97 at 08 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of yellow tan tissue  which is cut and sectioned to reveal a firm  gritty  tan white mass that is 0 6cm in greatest dimension with an ill defined border  No frozen section was done  The specimen has been submitted in its entirety in A B  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unifocal.
