Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Kristina Braaten  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Stitch at 12 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEVERAL FOCI AROUND THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   0 2 CM FROM THE MARGIN  SEE NOTE   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Results of hormone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm irregular tan white skin with an eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  At the 6 o clock aspect  2 0cm inferior to the nipple is a 6 0cm in length well healed linear scar  The posterior aspect is inked black and the anterior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity  consistent with a previous biopsy site at the 6 o clock aspect  which communicates with the deep posterior margin and comes to 1 0cm from the scar bearing skin surface  and 1 0cm from the 6 o clock blue inked anterior aspect  The cavity s lining is tan pink  smooth and glistening with friable  tan white chalky material  The remaining parenchyma consists of tan yellow lobulated unremarkable fibrofatty tissue with no masses or lesions grossly appreciated  At the lateral aspect no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire 6 o clock cavity to include the closest anterior margin and the exposed posterior aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Multifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA  Question of cancer by mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 4CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 0 2CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  AND WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  DefinIte blood vascular invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE  B  BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   1  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA HYPERPLASIA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The margins of resection are free of carcinoma  and atypical hyperplasia  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 2 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white area measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  0 2cm from the closest margin  A representative section from the suspicious area is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder of the lesion is in B D  Additional representative sections of the surrounding tissue are in E and F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and a 6 0cm sutured recent incision  The specimen is irregular  such that there is significantly more tissue in the superior lateral region  In addition  posterior to the ellipse  beneath the recent incision is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm apparently exposed biopsy cavity  which is inked green  The margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal soft white parenchyma in the region of the biopsy cavity  The closest margin to the biopsy site is 1cm  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty  with an area of localized fibrous and cystic change  1 0cm inferior and medial to the nipple  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted from medial to lateral in G K  with margin  Representative sections of the cystic area  medial to the biopsy cavity are in L and M  Unremarkable tissue away from the cavity is in N  The axillary tissue is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in O V  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unifocal.
