 a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  tan yellow  firm to rubbery piece of tissue  with needle localization  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  well demarcated  firm  white  round nodule with a central 0 6cm round  ill defined area of red gray cystic and hemorrhagic spaces measuring between 0 1cm to 0 2cm in diameter  The specimen is submitted in A through E  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH A MUCINOUS COMPONENT  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Unifocal.
