as of tan firmness surrounding  No discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the section containing the slightly firmer tissue adjacent to the central hemorrhage in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the section containing the metal clip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    M J   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior final shaved margins   are multiple fragments of tan pink  shaggy to shiny soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan pink  unremarkable cut surface  and is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan pink to yellow  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of pink brown  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral shaved final margins   are two fragments of tan brown to pink  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   are two fragments of red orange  shiny fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  Nine candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from 0 2cm to 1 2cm  are identified  The candidate lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four candidate lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left axilla contents   are multiple fragments of tan yellow  fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Two lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1 3cm in greatest dimension respectively  are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Attached fibroadipose tissue  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODE  LEFT A  report_end  , Multifocal_(multiple_within_same_quadrant).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA  Mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO A MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor cells display endocrine features  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue  containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan  well circumscribed nodule that abuts several margins  Representative sections of the nodule are submitted in A through C  representative sections of grossly unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in D and E  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  ABUTTING MARGIN  O R  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unifocal.
